  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Virginia recorded $2.5B in federal contract obligations for FY2027 to date. Award activity totaled 16,237 obligations with an average award size of $153K. Obligations fell 97.9% year over year, reflecting that current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date). Annual context shows prior full fiscal years at much larger levels: FY22 was $91.7B, FY23 was $109B, FY24 was $113B, FY25 was $124B, and FY26 was $121B. The Department of Veterans Affairs led buying in FY2027 to date with $1.4B, followed by the Department of Health and Human Services with $210M and the Department of Justice with $165M. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP was the largest vendor with $900M in obligations, and Direct Health and Medical Insurance Carriers was the largest industry at $900M. Computer Systems Design Services and Other Computer Related Services were also sizable industries with $511M and $343M respectively. This snapshot highlights a concentrated VA-driven health services profile in the current fiscal-year-to-date spending mix.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "How does FY2027 to date compare with recent full fiscal years?",
        "body": "FY2027 to date obligations were $2.5B. FY22 obligations were $91.7B, FY23 obligations were $109B, FY24 obligations were $113B, FY25 obligations were $124B, and FY26 obligations were $121B. Obligations fell 97.9% year over year, and current-year totals are partial (fiscal year to date)."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Which agencies and vendors account for most FY2027 to date obligations in Virginia?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $1.4B in FY2027 to date. The Department of Health and Human Services obligated $210M and the Department of Justice obligated $165M. TRIWEST HEALTHCARE ALLIANCE CORP received $900M, ACCENTURE FEDERAL SERVICES LLC received $232M, and GENERAL DYNAMICS INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY, INC. received $158M."
      }
    ]
  },
